{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/catalog/ghost_catalog.tex","new_string":"$r_N$ to stabilize at $\\lceil\\log_2 x_0\\rceil$ once $2^{B_N}>x_0$; a ghost\nrides the diagonal $r_N\\sim 2^{B_N}$. The bias is\n$|D_3|=\\bigl|\\frac1M\\sum_n \\zeta_3^{-b_n}-\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathrm{geom}}\n[\\zeta_3^{-b}]\\bigr|$, the order-3 non-coboundary two-point shadow.\n\n\\section{Translating between a word and the integer it represents}\n\n\\subsection*{Explanation}\nA word does not represent a single integer but a single \\emph{residue\nclass}: the set of odd $x$ whose first $M$ valuations equal\n$w=(b_0,\\dots,b_{M-1})$ is exactly one arithmetic progression\n\\[\nx\\equiv r \\pmod{2^{B_M+1}},\\qquad B_M=\\textstyle\\sum_{n<M}b_n ,\n\\]\nand ``the integer'' tabulated in this catalog is its least positive\nrepresentative $r$. Every member $r+k\\,2^{B_M+1}$ ($k\\ge0$) produces the\nsame first $M$ letters; the word sees only $x\\bmod 2^{B_M+1}$. The\nconverse direction is trivial: iterate\n$x\\mapsto(3x+1)/2^{v_2(3x+1)}$ and read the exponents.\n\n\\subsection*{Formula}\nAlong the prefix the orbit point has the exact affine form\n\\[\nx_n=\\frac{3^{\\,n}x_0+A_n}{2^{B_n}},\\qquad\nA_n=\\sum_{j<n}3^{\\,n-1-j}\\,2^{B_j},\\qquad B_n=\\sum_{j<n}b_j .\n\\]\nThe letter condition $v_2(3x_n+1)=b_n$ is the congruence\n\\[\n3^{\\,n+1}x_0+A_{n+1}\\equiv 2^{B_{n+1}}\\pmod{2^{B_{n+1}+1}}\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\nx_0\\equiv 3^{-(n+1)}\\bigl(2^{B_{n+1}}-A_{n+1}\\bigr)\n\\pmod{2^{B_{n+1}+1}},\n\\]\n($3$ is a unit in $\\mathbb Z_2$), so each letter appends $b_n$ new\nbinary digits of $x_0$: a Hensel-style lift. After $M$ letters the class\nmodulus is $2^{B_M+1}$ and $r$ is the lift's value reduced to\n$[1,2^{B_M+1})$.\n\n\\subsection*{Python}\nThe lift as implemented in \\texttt{search/frontier.py}\n(\\texttt{realize}); $r$ is built letter by letter:\n\\begin{verbatim}\ndef realize(bs):                       # word -> (r, B+1)\n    r, Mb = 1, 1                       # class rep and its bit-modulus\n    A = 0; B = 0; P3 = 1               # running A_n, B_n, 3^n\n    for b in bs:\n        need = B + b; mod = 1 << (need + 1)\n        c    = (3*A + (1 << B)) % mod          # A_{n+1} mod 2^{B+b+1}\n        x0   = (pow(3*P3, -1, mod)\n                * (((1 << need) - c) % mod)) % mod\n        if need + 1 > Mb:\n            r = x0; Mb = need + 1\n        A = 3*A + (1 << B); P3 *= 3; B += b\n    return r, Mb\n\ndef word_of(x, M):                     # integer -> word\n    out = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        t = 3*x + 1; b = (t & -t).bit_length() - 1\n        out.append(b); x = t >> b\n    return out\n\\end{verbatim}\n\n\\subsection*{Commands}\n\\begin{verbatim}\ncd shadow_frontier\n# word -> integer (paste the letters as one string)\npython3 -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'search'); \\\n  from frontier import realize; \\\n  w=[int(c) for c in '111411211121...']; \\\n  r,Mb=realize(w); print(r, r.bit_length(), Mb)\"\n# integer -> word, plus the four-panel candidate image\npython3 search/candidate_image.py --word 1,1,1,4,1,1,2,... --out viz/cand.png\npython3 search/candidate_image.py --seed 687871 --steps 55 --out viz/c687871.png\n\\end{verbatim}\n\n\\subsection*{Worked example: catalog word \\#1}\nFor the word \\#1 above ($M=240$, mean $1.583$, $|D_3|=0.214$):\n$B_M=380$, modulus $2^{381}$, and the least positive representative is\nthe $381$-bit integer\n\\begin{center}\\ttfamily\\small\n45276335476484047115725251008950986904354815513999907611\\\\\n28044450220436219657540681487193488995285987515743750727311\n\\end{center}\nwhose first $240$ Syracuse letters reproduce the word exactly\n(machine-checked). Its fill ratio is $r$'s bit length over $B_M+1$:\n$381/381=1.000$ --- and the half-word prefix already needs $184$ bits of\n$185$: the representative \\emph{grows with the prefix} ($184\\to381$\nbits from $M=120$ to $240$) instead of stabilizing. That diagonal ride\nis the ghost signature of the Conventions section: the class contains\nno positive integer below $2^{380}$. Contrast a true integer\nrealization: the survival champion $687871$ \\emph{is} the least\nrepresentative of its own $50$-letter class, and stays put as the\nprefix grows --- stabilization versus diagonal is the whole test.\n\n\\section{The 120 pilot candidates: statistics}","old_string":"$r_N$ to stabilize at $\\lceil\\log_2 x_0\\rceil$ once $2^{B_N}>x_0$; a ghost\nrides the diagonal $r_N\\sim 2^{B_N}$. The bias is\n$|D_3|=\\bigl|\\frac1M\\sum_n \\zeta_3^{-b_n}-\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathrm{geom}}\n[\\zeta_3^{-b}]\\bigr|$, the order-3 non-coboundary two-point shadow.\n\n\\section{The 120 pilot candidates: statistics}","replace_all":false}